<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">1971</h1><p class="ref-lede">1971 in world history: 20 events, 1 birth, 14 deaths, 2 works, 4 states founded and 4 that came to an end. 232 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/1967">1967</a><a href="/years/1968">1968</a><a href="/years/1969">1969</a><a href="/years/1970">1970</a><a href="/years/1971" aria-current="page">1971</a><a href="/years/1972">1972</a><a href="/years/1973">1973</a><a href="/years/1974">1974</a><a href="/years/1975">1975</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-25">25 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Idi Amin seizes power in Uganda</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">While President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milton-obote">Milton Obote</a> was abroad, army commander <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/idi-amin">Idi Amin</a> took power in a coup. His eight-year rule saw the expulsion of Uganda's Asians and the killing of an estimated 100,000 to 500,000 people.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-31">31 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Apollo 14 launches for the Moon</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Alan Shepard, Stuart Roosa and Edgar Mitchell lifted off from Kennedy Space Center. Landing at Fra Mauro on 5 February, Shepard famously hit two golf balls on the lunar surface.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-2">2 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Idi Amin proclaims himself President of Uganda</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">A week after his coup, Amin declared himself head of state and suspended parts of the constitution. His rule became one of the most brutal in post-colonial <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> until his overthrow in 1979.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-5">5 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Apollo 14 lands at Fra Mauro</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Alan Shepard and Edgar Mitchell landed in the lunar highlands, the target of the aborted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apollo">Apollo</a> 13. Shepard, America's first astronaut in space, became the fifth person to walk on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhu">Moon</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-8">8 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Joe Frazier beats Muhammad Ali in the 'Fight of the Century'</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">At Madison Square Garden, Frazier won a unanimous decision after knocking Ali down in the 15th round. It was Ali's first professional defeat.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-26">26 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Bangladesh declares independence from Pakistan</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">After the Pakistani army's crackdown in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dhaka">Dhaka</a>, independence was proclaimed in the name of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sheikh-mujibur-rahman">Sheikh Mujibur Rahman</a>. Nine months of war followed, and Bangladesh won its freedom in December 1971.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-31">31 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Apollo 15 astronauts drive the first rover on the Moon</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a> Scott and James Irwin took the battery-powered Lunar Roving Vehicle on its first drive near Hadley Rille. The rover let astronauts range much farther from their lander to collect samples.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-2">2 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The United Arab Emirates is founded</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Six of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trucial-states">Trucial States</a>, led by Abu Dhabi and Dubai, formed the United Arab <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirates</a> after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>'s withdrawal from the Gulf. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ras-al-khaimah">Ras al-Khaimah</a> joined in 1972.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/bangladesh-liberation-war" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bangladesh-liberation-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">War</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/bangladesh-liberation-war">Bangladesh Liberation War</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Bangladesh Liberation War was the conflict of 1971 in which East Pakistan won independence as Bangladesh.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/united-nations-general-assembly-resolution-2758">United Nations General Assembly Resolution 2758</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">United Nations General Assembly Resolution 2758, adopted on 25 October 1971, recognised the representatives of the People's Republic of China as the only lawful representatives of China at the United Nations.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/okinawa-reversion-agreement">Okinawa Reversion Agreement</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Okinawa Reversion Agreement was a treaty between the United States and Japan, signed on 17 June 1971, under which the Ryukyu Islands, administered by the United States since 1945, returned to Japanese sovereignty on 15 May 1972.</p></div></li></ol></section>
